CORE
main.go
--go-race-check --unwind 3 --unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[go::main\.main\.data-race\.1\] line 9 data race \(write\): SUCCESS$
^\[go::main\.main\.data-race\.\d+\] line 18 data race \(write\): FAILURE$
^\[go::main\.main\$lit1\.data-race\.1\] line 12 data race \(write\): FAILURE$
^\[go::main\.main\.data-race\.\d+\] line 20 data race \(write\): UNKNOWN$
^\[go::main\.main\.panic\.1\] line 22 panic: after: UNKNOWN$
^\[go::main\.main\$lit1\.panic\.1\] line 14 panic: in the goroutine: UNKNOWN$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^\[.*\]: SUCCESS.*line (1[2-9]|2[0-9]) .*$
^\[.*\] line (1[2-9]|2[0-9]) .*: SUCCESS$
^warning: ignoring
--
A data race is a fatal property: a racy read of a value of more than one word
may observe a torn value, which can corrupt memory arbitrarily. Properties
that may be checked after a race, in any goroutine, are UNKNOWN; the access
before the go statement keeps its status.
